Subject: [PATCH] foot: handle Darwin UTF-32 and thread names

Darwin uses 32-bit UTF-32 wchar_t like the BSDs but does not define
__STDC_ISO_10646__. It also exposes the one-argument pthread_setname_np()
form, so map foot's renderer helper to the Darwin signature.

diff -ruN -U0 --exclude=*.bak a/char32.c b/char32.c
--- a/char32.c	2026-05-14 23:26:04
+++ b/char32.c	2026-07-05 00:31:31
@@ -37 +37 @@
-#if (!defined(__STDC_ISO_10646__) || !__STDC_ISO_10646__) && !defined(__FreeBSD__) && !defined(__OpenBSD__)
+#if (!defined(__STDC_ISO_10646__) || !__STDC_ISO_10646__) && !defined(__FreeBSD__) && !defined(__OpenBSD__) && !defined(__APPLE__)
diff -ruN -U0 --exclude=*.bak a/render.c b/render.c
--- a/render.c	2026-05-14 23:26:04
+++ b/render.c	2026-07-05 00:31:31
@@ -17,0 +18,2 @@
+#elif defined(__APPLE__)
+ #define pthread_setname_np(thread, name) pthread_setname_np(name)
